  "body": "Found by the post-merge review of PR #1074 (merged 2026-11-12 as ec57632d).\n\nThe model page says \"Imported under a STEP facet budget of N\", but a re-import uses the window's session setting (`crates/ui/src/state_step_budget.rs`, about line 63, and the import start in `state.rs`), which resets to 30,000,000 at every launch. Reproduction: import a large STEP with the budget set to 60,000,000, restart the app, re-import the same file: it comes back under the default - coarsened and flagged reduced-fidelity, or refused as too large.\n\nWhy P2: nothing wrong is posted - a coarsened import is flagged and the gouge checks tighten - but the model silently changes fidelity on a re-import.\n\nDone means: a re-import of an existing model defaults to the budget recorded with that model (the user can still change it), pinned by a test; the same for the MCP and script re-import paths.",
